cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DORA Attestation Gatekeeper"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a supervisory gatekeeper for HSM attestation
  verification under DORA. Operated by the National Competent Authority,
  the gatekeeper executes a two-step verify/confirm protocol with the
  financial entity, signs receipts that are independently verifiable
  against pinned vendor trust anchors (Yubico, Marvell/Cavium, Microsoft
  Azure, Google Cloud HSM), maintains a hash-chained tamper-evident audit
  log, and enforces NCA-role-based authorisation. Version 1.2.0 added a
  settlement-time signature verification endpoint (POST /api/v1/verify)
  for use by settlement-rail enforcement components such as railgate.
  Version 1.4.0 fixes a start-up failure in 1.3.0 (duplicate key in
  application.yaml), moves the receipt wire format to v2 so that the
  confirmation nonce is inside the signed form (lockstep upgrade with hsm
  1.4.0 required), binds Step 7 confirmation to the jurisdiction in the
  path and to the mTLS principal that performed the verification, consumes
  the nonce atomically, makes settlement compliance follow the
  confirmation outcome, and caches chain-integrity checks behind a
  supervisor-only health endpoint. Version 1.5.0 makes the settlement
  contract with railgate work end to end by storing the certificate
  confirmed at Step 7 and resolving it from serial number and issuer DN
  (lockstep upgrade with hsm 1.5.0 and railgate 1.5.0 required), reads
  YubiHSM capabilities big-endian and rejects re-imported keys, makes every
  DORA article bit depend on a valid attestation signature, builds
  issuer-CA paths through intermediate certificates, and verifies audit-log
  integrity against the file on disk with the configured algorithm and
  retired keys. Supports the data-minimised quadruple-
  triangulation model: only digest, signature, and certificate identifiers
  traverse the supervisor boundary — transaction payload content is never
  exposed to the supervisor. Companions: hsm (financial-entity-side HSM
  attestation verification) and railgate (central-bank settlement-rail
  enforcement).
